analog_html='<!doctype html><meta charset="utf-8"><title>EventSpikeSeg140k GF180 — final</title><style>'+css+'</style><h1>EventSpikeSeg140k · GF180 analog</h1><aside>Final article package: full hierarchical research layout and representative consumption characterization. Spacious research atlas; no compact-die, manufacture, full-chip power or 5 ms signoff claim.</aside><h2>Layout and figures</h2><p><a href="layout/EventSpikeSeg140k_GF180_Analog.gds">Final GDS</a> · <a href="delivery.json">Delivery/inventory</a> · <a href="images/full_layout_overview.svg">Full-layout SVG</a> · <a href="images/plif_core_detail.svg">PLIF SVG</a> · <a href="images/membrane_bank_detail.svg">Membrane-bank SVG</a></p><img src="images/full_layout_overview.png" alt="Final research GDS hierarchy"><p>The overview simplifies small hierarchy extents. The PLIF view matches assembled GDS geometry; the membrane-bank close-up uses its qualified source-component GDS.</p><h2>Consumption</h2><p><a href="consumption/summary.json">Complete consumption data</a> · <a href="consumption/inventory.json">22-family coverage</a> · <a href="package_manifest.json">Retained files and hashes</a></p><p>Per-instance native transients, reused rail currents, RMS DC samples and routed-library digital estimates remain distinct. Operation energy includes standing bias. Do not sum overlapping core/submodule/bank/whole-tile rows or charge shared cores to every logical membrane. The full 1024-state reader has partition/leaf consumption evidence only.</p><table><tr><th>Physical circuit</th><th>Window</th><th>Duration (µs)</th><th>Mean VDD (µW)</th><th>VDD energy (pJ)</th><th>Evidence basis</th></tr>'+''.join(rows)+'</table><h2>Archive and reproducibility</h2><p>Original source evidence is unchanged in evidence/ and components/. Historical paths are resolved through <code>artifacts/asic_artifact_index.json</code>. Superseded attempts, bulk build environments and historical intermediate databases are preserved in <code>'+html.escape(archive_root)+'</code>. Historical scripts may require restored paths/dependencies before replay; new runs should use a separate work directory.</p>'
