section=f'''\n\n## ASIC artifact reorganization — 2026-10-14\n\nCanonical article package: `artifacts/analog_asic/final/` (start at index.html). Final GDS is `layout/EventSpikeSeg140k_GF180_Analog.gds`; PNG/SVG figures are together in images/; current consumption data is consumption/summary.json. Original manifests/source/results are preserved unchanged under evidence/, components/, model_reference/support locations. The current path locator is `artifacts/asic_artifact_index.json`.\n\nDigital documentation-only snapshots are `artifacts/ASIC/final/` and `artifacts/ASIC_XL/final/`; neither claims a completed digital full-chip layout. Last exports, hierarchy inventory, completed block views and final reports are retained; digital jobs remain paused.\n\nAll superseded attempts and build environments moved to `{archive_root}/`, including related digital OpenROAD history. No files deleted. cleanup_plan.json inventories every original file; integrity_audit.json accounts for all{plan['original_file_count']:,} originals and verifies SHA256 of all{len(verified):,} retained files. restore_artifacts.ps1 can restore original artifact trees; pre-cleanup docs and .gitignore are backed up in the same bin. User review of this bin is pending; do not delete it without explicit instruction. Historical report/script paths are original provenance; resolve with the locator or restore dependencies before replay. New experiments belong outside final/.\n'''
active=f'''# Active tasks\n\nUpdated2026-10-14. Article layout, representative consumption and PNG/SVG views are delivered.\n\n## Current deliverables\n\n- Analog article package: `artifacts/analog_asic/final/index.html`.\n- Final hierarchical GDS: `artifacts/analog_asic/final/layout/EventSpikeSeg140k_GF180_Analog.gds` (537,103,416bytes; SHA256fb28eeb6bbc8901ad8594dcd4b5cc14450b7cae438bd5f239096c587f96d1d92).\n- Figures: `artifacts/analog_asic/final/images/`, including the three true-vectorSVGs and PNGs.\n- Consumption: `artifacts/analog_asic/final/consumption/summary.json`,22 required families/74 rows. Per-instance transients, reused rail traces, RMS DC samples and digital-library estimates are explicitly distinguished.\n- Digital140k andXL documentation: `artifacts/ASIC/final/index.html` and `artifacts/ASIC_XL/final/index.html`. No digital full-chip completion claimed.\n\n## Scope and limitations\n\nOriginal epoch58 full-float analog topology and54,630,400 state identities including30,976,000 membranes remain preserved. External analog/control interfaces are documented. The full1024-state page lacks complete connected power/transient evidence; partition and leaf consumption are supplied. No compact die, calibrated accuracy, full-chip power, globalRC/IR/EM, manufacture or full-population5ms acceptance is claimed. Further circuit optimization is optional.\n\n## Cleanup completed; user bin review pending\n\nReview bin: `{archive_root}/`. All{plan['original_file_count']:,} original files accounted for; retained originals are SHA256-verified. No deletions performed. Original evidence bytes/hashes are preserved; `artifacts/asic_artifact_index.json` maps old paths to retained or binned files. restore_artifacts.ps1 and the move inventory are in the bin. Do not delete the bin without explicit user instruction. Archive the seven docs before future edits. No new simulations or Docker images were started during cleanup.\n'''
